{
 "_about": "One action table for the three harnesses (review finding F6), version 3. generate.py builds the Claude permission arrays, the delegate settings fragment and the Codex rules file from it, and fails when a family lacks an entry or a stated reason for any harness. Grok reads the Claude command rules from .claude/settings.json (grok-build f0e3be11: xai-grok-workspace/src/permission/resolution.rs:28-68). Text rules are defense in depth: exec-guard parses the unwrapped argv for every family here (proposal v3, section 3), and the guard hooks fail closed (departure D8).",
 "families": [
  {
   "id": "privilege",
   "decision": "deny",
   "why": "The operator runs privileged commands personally (settled S15 rung 4; operator decision D5 of 2026-09-28: block, including wrapped forms and `osascript ... with administrator privileges`).",
   "claude": [
    "Bash(sudo *)",
    "Bash(su *)",
    "Bash(doas *)",
    "Bash(pkexec *)",
    "Bash(gsudo *)",
    "Bash(runas *)",
