    "PowerShell(*-Verb RunAs*)",
    "Bash(env sudo *)",
    "Bash(env * sudo *)",
    "Bash(env su *)",
    "Bash(env * su *)",
    "Bash(env doas *)",
    "Bash(env * doas *)",
    "Bash(env pkexec *)",
    "Bash(env * pkexec *)",
    "Bash(osascript *with administrator privileges*)",
    "Bash(*/osascript *with administrator privileges*)"
   ],
   "codex": [
    {
     "pattern": [
      [
       "sudo",
       "su",
       "doas",
       "pkexec",
       "gsudo",
       "runas"
      ]
     ],
     "match": [
      "sudo true",
      "doas reboot"
     ],
     "not_match": [
      "sudoku --help"
     ]
    },
    {
     "pattern": [
      [
       "/usr/bin/sudo",
       "/bin/sudo",
       "/usr/local/bin/sudo",
       "/bin/su",
       "/usr/bin/su",
       "/usr/bin/doas",
       "/usr/local/bin/doas",
       "/usr/bin/pkexec"
      ]
     ],
     "match": [
      "/usr/bin/sudo true"
     ]
    },
    {
     "pattern": [
      "env",
      [
       "sudo",
       "su",
       "doas",
       "pkexec"
      ]
     ],
     "match": [
      "env sudo true"
     ],
     "not_match": [
      "env cargo test"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "codex_note": "Codex matches argv exactly and splits plain `bash -lc` scripts before matching (docs: rules, 'Shell wrappers and compound commands'), so `bash -lc 'sudo -n id'` is forbidden. `env -i sudo`, other absolute paths and interpreter calls are left to exec-guard's unwrapper. `osascript -e '... with administrator privileges'` arrives as one `-e` string; exec-guard carries it."
  },
  {
   "id": "publish",
   "decision": "deny",
   "why": "Publishing is outward and irreversible. The operator publishes from a terminal; no agent session publishes (settled S19, rung 4 of S15). A gist is publication of content, and the current token carries the `gist` scope.",
